  "conclusions": [
    "All five accepted runner records are reachable in the positively weighted easy band for fresh eligible candidates.",
    "Zero-weight bands are excluded. No rated fallback is invented when a positively weighted band is empty. Unrated fallback is uniform; missing policy chooses minimum ID.",
    "History exclusions remove only explicitly excluded items; within a supported band selection does not inspect answer values, templates, positions, roles or generation metadata.",
    "Thus any positive easy-band weight preserves support of its remaining decision cases; weights change frequency, and history can exhaust cases."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No live learner policy/history is in the captured inventory. Runs cover branches and support conditional on specified histories/weights, not a prediction of an actual future learner session.",
    "Temporary monotone entity IDs for not-yet-published records are a read-only model. Actual allocated IDs can change individual seeded draws, but not the uniform in-band support or answer independence.",
    "Concurrent publication can change inventory from basis 5275."
  ]
